---
import Divider from "../../../../components/ui/Divider.astro";
import Layout from "../../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { Code } from "astro-expressive-code/components";

//#region CodeSnippets
const Q1 = `for (let i = 0; i < 5; i++) {
  console.log(i);
}`;
const Q2 = `let total = 0;

for (let i = 1; i <= 4; i++) {
  total = total + i;
}`;
const Q3 = `i ← 1

REPEAT 3 TIMES
{
  DISPLAY(i)
  i ← i + 1
}`;
//#endregion
---

<Layout>
  <div class="container my-4">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-sm-12 col-md-10">
        <a href="/courses/ap-csp/" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-light mb-3">
          <i class="si-arrow-left"></i> Back
        </a>

        <h1>Question Set 5</h1>

        <h4 class="text-sn-theme">
          Six questions &middot; 11 minutes &middot; cumulative
        </h4>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="mb-5" />

        <section id="objective">
          <h2>What This Is</h2>

          <p>Five exam-style questions covering Activity 1.1 through 1.20, weighted toward <b>counted loops and loop patterns</b>. The reference sheet has no <code>for</code> loop, and two of these are about what it has instead.</p>

          <p>
            <b>Set a timer for 11 minutes.</b> Work them out on paper; do not run
            the code. Mark each answer <b>sure</b> or <b>unsure</b>. Guess
            rather than leave a blank &mdash; the AP exam has no penalty for a
            wrong answer.
          </p>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="questions">
          <h2>The Questions</h2>

          <p>
            Four have exactly one correct answer, one asks you to select
            <i>all</i> that apply, and the last is about data or the impact of
            computing rather than about code. <b>Thirteen of the exam's seventy
            questions look like that last one</b>, so it is on every set from
            here on.
          </p>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Question 1</h3>

          <p>How many times does this loop body run?</p>

          <Code
            code={Q1}
            frame="code"
            lang="javascript"
            title="Question 1"
            showLineNumbers={false}
            class="mb-3"
          />

          <ul>
            <li>(A) <code>4</code></li>
            <li>(B) <code>5</code></li>
            <li>(C) <code>6</code></li>
            <li>(D) <code>0</code></li>
          </ul>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Question 2</h3>

          <p>What does <code>total</code> hold after this runs?</p>

          <Code
            code={Q2}
            frame="code"
            lang="javascript"
            title="Question 2"
            showLineNumbers={false}
            class="mb-3"
          />

          <ul>
            <li>(A) <code>4</code></li>
            <li>(B) <code>10</code></li>
            <li>(C) <code>0</code></li>
            <li>(D) <code>24</code></li>
          </ul>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Question 3</h3>

          <p>What does this display?</p>

          <Code
            code={Q3}
            frame="code"
            lang="txt"
            title="Question 3 — exam notation"
            showLineNumbers={false}
            class="mb-3"
          />

          <ul>
            <li>(A) <code>1 2 3</code></li>
            <li>(B) <code>0 1 2</code></li>
            <li>(C) <code>3 3 3</code></li>
            <li>(D) <code>1 1 1</code></li>
          </ul>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Question 4</h3>

          <p>Why does the program above need the line <code>i &larr; i + 1</code> at all?</p>

          <ul>
            <li>(A) To stop the loop after three passes.</li>
            <li>(B) Because <code>REPEAT n TIMES</code> provides no counter variable of its own.</li>
            <li>(C) Because <code>DISPLAY</code> cannot show a variable that does not change.</li>
            <li>(D) It is not needed; the program works without it.</li>
          </ul>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Question 5 &mdash; Select all that apply</h3>

          <p>Which of these are true about a <b>running maximum</b> loop that finds the largest value?</p>

          <ul>
            <li>(A) It needs a variable set up before the loop starts</li>
            <li>(B) It compares each value against the current best</li>
            <li>(C) It must sort the values first</li>
            <li>(D) It updates the best value only when it finds a larger one</li>
            <li>(E) It requires a nested loop</li>
          </ul>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Question 6 &mdash; Data and Impact</h3>

          <p>A school moves all homework submission online. Which is the clearest example of the <b>digital divide</b> affecting this decision?</p>

          <ul>
            <li>(A) Some students prefer paper</li>
            <li>(B) The school's website is slow at peak hours</li>
            <li>(C) Students without reliable home internet cannot submit on time</li>
            <li>(D) Teachers must learn a new system</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="submit">
          <h2>Submit</h2>

          <p>
            Six answers, each marked <b>sure</b> or <b>unsure</b>, plus how far
            you got when the timer went off. Worth <b>2 points</b>, graded on
            completion.
          </p>
        </section>

        <h1
          class="text-center mt-5 text-sn-theme border border-primary slow-flash"
        >
          Start the Timer
        </h1>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
